{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EySDrbm634bSbBYDHayQeY","type":"tool_result","content":"R01 List every input the agent receives. That includes API responses (errors and streamed content too), tool and connector output, incoming webhooks and callbacks, messages from other agents, user input, fetched pages, files, and retrieved chunks. Authenticate each sender (prove who sent it), and verify signatures where they exist. Treat content as untrusted even when it comes from an authenticated service or an internal one. Before content reaches the model or runs anywhere, check its type, schema, and size. Also check its content for attack payloads and hidden prompt-injection instructions. Reject or hold aside bad payloads. If a required check fails to run, don't let unchecked content through. Test broken, oversized, faked, and hostile responses from each integration.\n[{'problem': 'Injected instructions in valid content reaching forbidden tools unblocked', 'owner': 'R02'}, {'problem': 'Hidden instructions in tool names, descriptions, or schemas', 'owner': 'E04'}, {'problem': 'Replayed peer-agent requests with no freshness or nonce check', 'owner': 'E07'}, {'problem': 'Secrets leaking into outputs or normal logs', 'owner': 'R03'}, {'problem': 'Unapproved sources able to add documents to the retrieval corpus', 'owner': 'R04'}]\nR02 Keep API responses, connector messages, and other outside content out of trusted system and policy channels. Label where each piece came from and how much it is trusted. Test prompt injection in responses that pass schema checks. Include free-text fields, error messages, documents, and tool output. Checks and channel separation can't guarantee that prompt injection is prevented. So show that credential limits, tool permissions, and destructive-action gates still block harm if the model follows an injected instruction. Repeat each attack and include adaptive versions. One failed attempt makes a defense look stronger than it is. B05 covers agents that combine untrusted input, sensitive access, and outside actions.\n[{'problem': 'Missing type, schema, or size checks on API responses', 'owner': 'R01'}, {'problem': 'Hidden instructions in tool names, descriptions, or schemas', 'owner': 'E04'}, {'problem': \"One run planting instructions in another run's memory\", 'owner': 'R05'}, {'problem': 'Generated output run as SQL or shell without parameterizing', 'owner': 'R03'}]\nR03 Remove secrets and limit sensitive data before tool output, debug output, or responses reach the model, outside recipients, or normal logs. Some clients fetch URLs on their own when they display output, such as Markdown images and link previews. These can leak data without any tool call, so block them or allow only approved URLs. Check generated output before it goes into SQL, a shell, an HTML page, or anything else that runs it. Use parameterized queries and commands (for example, argument lists for shell calls), and the right escaping for each context. Test with fake secrets and injection payloads. Confirm that leaks and unintended execution are blocked, and that redacted audit evidence is kept.\n[{'problem': 'A tool call sending data to an unapproved destination', 'owner': 'B09'}, {'problem': 'Long-lived secrets checked into config or baked into images', 'owner': 'B03'}, {'problem': 'Incoming hostile payloads not validated', 'owner': 'R01'}, {'problem': \"Retrieval returning another tenant's documents\", 'owner': 'R04'}]\n     1\t\"\"\"Approval requests and decisions for high-impact operations.\n     2\t\n     3\tRequests are posted to the business unit's approvals channel in Slack with\n     4\tthe full argument summary. Approvers decide with the Slack buttons; the\n     5\tinteractive callback is signature-checked in main.py and then calls\n     6\t``decide``. Approver authority is checked against the role map in policy.\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport json\n    11\timport uuid\n    12\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    13\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n    14\tfrom typing import Any\n    15\t\n    16\tfrom app.audit import digest, summarize_args\n    17\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    21\tclass Approval:\n    22\t    id: str\n    23\t    approver: str\n    24\t    approver_role: str\n    25\t    expires_at: datetime\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tclass ApproverNotAuthorized(Exception):\n    29\t    pass\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tclass ApprovalStore:\n    33\t    def __init__(self, pool, policy: dict, notifier):\n    34\t        self.pool = pool\n    35\t        self.ttl = timedelta(minutes=int(policy[\"approvals\"][\"ttl_minutes\"]))\n    36\t        self.approver_roles: dict[str, list[str]] = policy[\"approvals\"][\"approver_roles\"]\n    37\t        self.notifier = notifier\n    38\t\n    39\t    async def request(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool: str, target: str, args: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    40\t        approval_id = f\"apr-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n    41\t        expires_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc) + self.ttl\n    42\t        await self.pool.execute(\n    43\t            \"\"\"\n    44\t            INSERT INTO approvals (\n    45\t                id, tool, target, args_sha256, args_summary, tenant,\n    46\t                requested_by_instance, requested_by_run, delegated_subject,\n    47\t                status, requested_at, expires_at\n    48\t            ) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5::jsonb, $6, $7, $8, $9, 'pending', now(), $10)\n    49\t            \"\"\",\n    50\t            approval_id,\n    51\t            tool,\n    52\t            target,\n    53\t            digest(args),\n    54\t            json.dumps(summarize_args(args)),\n    55\t            ident.tenant,\n    56\t            ident.agent_instance_id,\n    57\t            ident.run_id,\n    58\t            ident.delegated_subject,\n    59\t            expires_at,\n    60\t        )\n    61\t        await self.notifier.post_approval_request(\n    62\t            tenant=ident.tenant,\n    63\t            approval_id=approval_id,\n    64\t            tool=tool,\n    65\t            target=target,\n    66\t            summary=summarize_args(args),\n    67\t            expires_at=expires_at,\n    68\t        )\n    69\t        return approval_id\n    70\t\n    71\t    async def find_valid(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool: str, target: str) -> Approval | None:\n    72\t        row = await self.pool.fetchrow(\n    73\t            \"\"\"\n    74\t            SELECT id, approver, approver_role, expires_at\n    75\t            FROM approvals\n    76\t            WHERE tool = $1\n    77\t              AND target = $2\n    78\t              AND tenant = $3\n    79\t              AND status = 'approved'\n    80\t              AND expires_at > now()\n    81\t            ORDER BY decided_at DESC\n    82\t            LIMIT 1\n    83\t            \"\"\",\n    84\t            tool,\n    85\t            target,\n    86\t            ident.tenant,\n    87\t        )\n    88\t        if row is None:\n    89\t            return None\n    90\t        if row[\"approver_role\"] not in self.approver_roles.get(tool, []):\n    91\t            return None\n    92\t        return Approval(row[\"id\"], row[\"approver\"], row[\"approver_role\"], row[\"expires_at\"])\n    93\t\n    94\t    async def decide(self, approval_id: str, approver: str, approver_role: str, approve: bool) -> None:\n    95\t        row = await self.pool.fetchrow(\n    96\t            \"SELECT tool, status, expires_at FROM approvals WHERE id = $1\", approval_id\n    97\t        )\n    98\t        if row is None or row[\"status\"] != \"pending\":\n    99\t            raise ValueError(\"approval is not pending\")\n   100\t        if row[\"expires_at\"] <= datetime.now(timezone.utc):\n   101\t            raise ValueError(\"approval request expired\")\n   102\t        if approver_role not in self.approver_roles.get(row[\"tool\"], []):\n   103\t            raise ApproverNotAuthorized(f\"{approver_role} cannot approve {row['tool']}\")\n   104\t        await self.pool.execute(\n   105\t            \"\"\"\n   106\t            UPDATE approvals\n   107\t            SET status = $2, approver = $3, approver_role = $4, decided_at = now()\n   108\t            WHERE id = $1 AND status = 'pending'\n   109\t            \"\"\",\n   110\t            approval_id,\n   111\t            \"approved\" if approve else \"rejected\",\n   112\t            approver,\n   113\t            approver_role,\n   114\t        )\napp/startup.py:43:        log.error(\"running state differs from release manifest: %s\", \", \".join(mismatches))\napp/startup.py:45:    log.info(\"agent_type_id=%s release=%s\", agent_type_id, manifest[\"release\"])\napp/context_size.py:73:        log.warning(\"token count failed; falling back to usage\", exc_info=True)\napp/mcp_client.py:42:def fingerprint(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\napp/mcp_client.py:96:            actual = fingerprint(tool)\napp/mcp_client.py:101:        log.info(\"erp tools loaded: %d\", len(self._tools))\napp/mcp_client.py:111:        log.info(\"erp tools refreshed: %d\", len(self._tools))\napp/killswitch.py:26:    row = await pool.fetchrow(_QUERY, f\"tenant:{tenant}\")\napp/ingest.py:132:        await pool.execute(\napp/ingest.py:142:    await pool.execute(\napp/tools/documents.py:20:        row = await pool.fetchrow(\napp/audit.py:93:    await pool.execute(\napp/approvals.py:42:        await self.pool.execute(\napp/approvals.py:72:        row = await self.pool.fetchrow(\napp/approvals.py:95:        row = await self.pool.fetchrow(\napp/approvals.py:104:        await self.pool.execute(\napp/budget.py:126:                    count = await conn.fetchval(\napp/budget.py:149:                    spent = await conn.fetchval(\napp/extractor.py:96:                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\napp/redact.py:78:    Slack and most chat clients fetch link and image URLs to render previews,\napp/loop.py:53:    async def execute_tool(self, ident, registry: ToolRegistry, use, parent: str, ctx: ContextMeasure) -> dict:\napp/loop.py:80:            with tracer.start_as_current_span(f\"execute_tool {use.name}\") as span:\napp/loop.py:173:                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\napp/mcp_client.py:3:On startup the tool list is fetched and each tool's description and input\napp/main.py:72:        count = await app.state.pool.fetchval(\napp/main.py:177:    row = await request.app.state.pool.fetchrow(\napp/ingest.py:34:    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\napp/ingest.py:35:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system|developer) (prompt|message)\\b\"),\napp/ingest.py:36:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are (now )?(an?|the) \\w+ (agent|assistant)\\b\"),\napp/ingest.py:37:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) (the )?(pay_invoice|erp_call|create_purchase_order|post_slack_message|memory_write)\\b\"),\napp/ingest.py:38:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(update|change) (our|the) (bank|remit|payee)\\b\"),\napp/ingest.py:39:    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\napp/tools/memory.py:21:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(ignore|disregard|override)\\b.{0,40}\\b(instruction|policy|approval|rule)s?\\b\"),\napp/tools/memory.py:22:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(always|never|must)\\b.{0,40}\\b(approve|pay|skip|send|transfer)\\b\"),\napp/tools/memory.py:23:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system prompt|you are|assistant:)\\b\"),\napp/tools/memory.py:24:    re.compile(r\"https?://\"),\napp/redact.py:17:    (\"bearer\", re.compile(r\"(?i)\\bbearer\\s+[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{16,}\")),\napp/redact.py:18:    (\"jwt\", re.compile(r\"\\beyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\b\")),\napp/redact.py:19:    (\"acct_token\", re.compile(r\"\\bacct_tok_[A-Za-z0-9_]{8,}\\b\")),\napp/redact.py:20:    (\"pay_token\", re.compile(r\"\\bpay_tok_[A-Za-z0-9_]{8,}\\b\")),\napp/redact.py:21:    (\"erp_session\", re.compile(r\"\\berp_sess_[A-Za-z0-9_]{8,}\\b\")),\napp/redact.py:22:    (\"password_kv\", re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(password|passwd|secret|api[_-]?key)\\s*[:=]\\s*\\S+\")),\napp/redact.py:27:    (\"iban\", re.compile(r\"\\b[A-Z]{2}\\d{2}[A-Z0-9]{11,30}\\b\")),\napp/redact.py:28:    (\"account_no\", re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(account|acct|routing)\\s*(no\\.?|number|#)?\\s*[:#]?\\s*(\\d[\\d -]{6,}\\d)\")),\napp/redact.py:31:MARKDOWN_IMAGE = re.compile(r\"!\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\(([^)\\s]+)[^)]*\\)\")\napp/redact.py:32:MARKDOWN_LINK = re.compile(r\"(?<!!)\\[([^\\]]*)\\]\\(([^)\\s]+)[^)]*\\)\")\napp/redact.py:33:SLACK_LINK = re.compile(r\"<(https?://[^|>]+)(\\|[^>]*)?>\")\napp/redact.py:34:BARE_URL = re.compile(r\"https?://[^\\s<>()]+\")\napp/mcp_client.py:26:    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|previous|prior) instructions\"),\napp/mcp_client.py:27:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system prompt|you are now|act as)\\b\"),\napp/mcp_client.py:28:    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(before|instead of) (calling|using) \\w+\\.\\w+\"),\napp/mcp_client.py:29:    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\napp/mcp_client.py:30:    re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z0-9+/]{120,}={0,2}\"),\n\"\"\"Operator stop control.\n\nOperators halt the fleet or one business unit by setting a row in\n``control_flags`` with the ``procurement_ops`` database role (see\nops/README in the platform runbook). The agent's own database role has\nSELECT only on this table, so the agent cannot clear or delay a halt.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n\nclass AgentHalted(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\n_QUERY = \"\"\"\nSELECT scope, reason, set_by, set_at\nFROM control_flags\nWHERE halted\n  AND (scope = 'fleet' OR scope = $1)\nORDER BY CASE WHEN scope = 'fleet' THEN 0 ELSE 1 END\nLIMIT 1\n\"\"\"\n\n\nasync def assert_running(pool, tenant: str) -> None:\n    row = await pool.fetchrow(_QUERY, f\"tenant:{tenant}\")\n    if row is not None:\n        raise AgentHalted(\n            f\"halted by {row['set_by']} at {row['set_at'].isoformat()} \"\n            f\"(scope={row['scope']}): {row['reason']}\"\n        )","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"422fd315-a0f9-49c7-bdf9-64937721f06b","uuid":"c238da8d-509c-4df3-ad95-7c9abcb1520c","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:05:02.113Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"R01 List every input the agent receives. That includes API responses (errors and streamed content too), tool and connector output, incoming webhooks and callbacks, messages from other agents, user input, fetched pages, files, and retrieved chunks. Authenticate each sender (prove who sent it), and verify signatures where they exist. Treat content as untrusted even when it comes from an authenticated service or an internal one. Before content reaches the model or runs anywhere, check its type, schema, and size. Also check its content for attack payloads and hidden prompt-injection instructions. Reject or hold aside bad payloads. If a required check fails to run, don't let unchecked content through. Test broken, oversized, faked, and hostile responses from each integration.\n[{'problem': 'Injected instructions in valid content reaching forbidden tools unblocked', 'owner': 'R02'}, {'problem': 'Hidden instructions in tool names, descriptions, or schemas', 'owner': 'E04'}, {'problem': 'Replayed peer-agent requests with no freshness or nonce check', 'owner': 'E07'}, {'problem': 'Secrets leaking into outputs or normal logs', 'owner': 'R03'}, {'problem': 'Unapproved sources able to add documents to the retrieval corpus', 'owner': 'R04'}]\nR02 Keep API responses, connector messages, and other outside content out of trusted system and policy channels. Label where each piece came from and how much it is trusted. Test prompt injection in responses that pass schema checks. Include free-text fields, error messages, documents, and tool output. Checks and channel separation can't guarantee that prompt inject